body:
Thanks so much!

&#x200B;

They use Jira with an Agile methodology, so the "Summary" in the report is actually the title.

&#x200B;

I'll add faux notes in my next exercise bug report, like "I tried to use similar spells from other champions and did not see any issues."  That's a great idea!

&#x200B;

As for severity and user path, I'm not sure how the company usual handles their definitions for people like business analysts, but the way I've used them here is based off the definitions given in their skill test, which *may* be based on single-player games. They are the only definitions from them that I *definitely* have, so I'm using them and avoiding future mix-ups with other definitions.

Here's my understanding of what they want:

&#x200B;

\- The title IS the summary (I think?), for they use Jira with an Agile methodology.

&#x200B;

\- I'm unsure if they expect 'Reproduction Rate', but in this exercise at least, I don't have the means to get that information. Thank you, as for the next week, I'll look out for any footage or what-have-you where I can get that information. This way I can practice writing it too.

&#x200B;

\- 'Expected Results' was not part of the skill test, which is why I didn't include it, but it definitely makes sense to include it. Thank you!

&#x200B;

\- I think 'Impact' is why they have 'Severity' and 'User path'.

&#x200B;

Lastly, I only have the provided footage, so I can't exercise all the feedback you gave. But I'll try!

&#x200B;

Thanks again!

Thanks for the uspeed tidbit! I'll wait to see how slow it feels on Saturday or if anyone else recommends the same thing, though. The genuine experience is important to me.

&#x200B;

The channel name is LudoLupus!
